From: junkyard
Subject: [PATCH] gs: port gs201 drivers to android-mainline

One cumulative patch, kept in two sections: the 6.1 -> 6.18 port this
project first needed for GrapheneOS's 6.18 GKI, then 6.18 -> android-mainline.

== 6.1 -> 6.18 ==
(gs: port the gs101/gs201-era SoC drivers to Linux 6.18)

Port private/google-modules/soc/gs to the GrapheneOS Linux 6.18 GKI for the gs201 lynx build.
Mechanical API migrations, no intended behaviour change:

  - platform_driver.remove returns void (6.11)
  - gpio_chip.set returns int (6.17)
  - strlcpy() removed, use strscpy() (6.8)
  - del_timer*() renamed timer_delete*() (6.15)
  - from_timer() renamed timer_container_of() (6.16)
  - hrtimer_init() replaced by hrtimer_setup() (6.15)
  - of_property_for_each_u32() takes 3 arguments (6.11)
  - tracepoint __assign_str() takes only the field (6.10)
  - MODULE_IMPORT_NS() takes a string literal (6.13)
  - <asm/unaligned.h> moved to <linux/unaligned.h> (6.12)
  - spi_master renamed spi_controller
  - PWM chips allocated with pwmchip_alloc() (6.9)
  - IOMMU ops: domain_alloc_paging/map_pages/unmap_pages, no fwspec->ops
  - iommu_register_device_fault_handler() removed (6.8): use the pixel_iommu fault registry that samsung_iommu.ko exports
  - iommu_domain_alloc(bus) replaced by iommu_paging_domain_alloc(dev) (6.11)
  - thermal core: trips live in thermal_trip_desc, tz->ops embedded, trip getters removed (gs_thermal_compat.h)
  - serial core: circ_buf replaced by the xmit_fifo kfifo (6.10)
  - V4L2: vidioc_queryctrl/g_ctrl/s_ctrl removed (6.18), served via ext-ctrls adapters
  - vb2: q->num_buffers replaced by vb2_get_num_buffers() (6.8)
  - v4l2_fh_add/del take the struct file (6.18)
  - driver_override moved into struct device (6.18)
  - sysfs bin_attribute callbacks take a const attribute (6.13+)
  - devm_device_add_groups() removed (6.11)
  - nr_irqs replaced by irq_get_nr_irqs() (6.13)
  - task->thread_group removed
  - dynamic BRK hooks removed (6.17)
  - relax -Wmissing-prototypes (on by default since 6.8, fatal with CONFIG_WERROR) for this vendor code
  - SPI: per-device chipselect accessors, is_dma_mapped removed

110 files.

lynx-only (kernel/patches-lynx/): felix builds the 6.1 tree these
drivers were written for.

== 6.18 -> android-mainline ==

Linux 6.18 ->
android-mainline (7.3). Only what lynx's gs201_soc / ext_modules build was
changed (plus a few non-gs201 siblings of the same files, for consistency).

Mechanical API migration (each mirrors the upstream conversion):
  * syscore: register_syscore_ops() -> register_syscore(struct syscore);
    callbacks take void *data (bts, pinctrl-samsung, exynos-pm, s3c2410_wdt).
  * clk: clk_ops.round_rate removed. composite.c hangs a determine_rate
    adapter (JY_CLK_DETERMINE_FROM_ROUND) off each existing round_rate.
  * dma_map_ops.map_page/unmap_page (+ map_resource) -> map_phys/unmap_phys
    (pcie-exynos-rc, dwc-whi).
  * iommu_domain_ops.attach_dev gained the old domain (samsung-iommu{,-v9}).
  * dwc PCIe: PCIE_ATU_TYPE_CFG0 -> PCIE_TLP_TYPE_CFG0_RDWR (aliased);
    dw_pcie_rp.use_linkup_irq removed -- see below.
  * pm_runtime_put() returns void (sbb-mux, dwc3-exynos, gsa_mbox).
  * in_irq() -> in_hardirq(); vmalloc_nr_pages() -> NR_VMALLOC; alarm
    timer API (alarm_start_timer(), void callbacks); hrtimer_setup();
    of_node_to_fwnode() -> of_fwnode_handle(); <linux/hex.h>;
    drivers/devfreq/governor.h -> <linux/devfreq-governor.h>;
    {devm_,}thermal_of_cooling_device_register() cdev_id (0) and the devm
    variant's dropped np; cpufreq_policy.{min,max}_freq_req embedded;
    RESERVEDMEM_OF_DECLARE() ops table; HCC_MAX_PSA() -> GET_MAX_PSA_SIZE();
    __platform_driver_register() mod_name; dma_fence lock accessors;
    vb2 wait_prepare/wait_finish removed (MFC/SMFC set vb2_queue.lock to the
    mutex those callbacks dropped).
  * UFS: ufshcd_lrb is the SCSI command's private data now and the
    android_vh_ufs_{fill_prdt,prepare,send,compl}_command hooks pass the
    scsi_cmnd. ufs-pixel's stats/trace helpers take the command
    (ufshcd_is_scsi_cmd() replaces "lrbp->cmd != NULL"); the fill_prdt
    handlers derive lrbp with scsi_cmd_priv(). ACK's
    ufshcd_bkops_ctrl_threshold() is emulated via hba->urgent_bkops_lvl +
    ufshcd_bkops_ctrl().
  * backlight Kbuild: EXTRA_CFLAGS (no longer honoured by kbuild) -> ccflags-y.

Behavioural decisions (also see gs201_defconfig / BUILD.bazel in the
devices/google/gs201 patch, which turns the dropped modules off):
  * Pixel vendor-hook ("vh") modules built on ACK-only infrastructure are
    not built (vh_sched & co, vh_fs, vh_cgroup, vh_thermal, pixel_em,
    pixel_metrics, smra, iovad-vendor-hooks, ufs-pixel-fips140, zram_gs +
    zcomp_*). This patch keeps their consumers compiling: vh_thermal's
    genl filter in gs_tmu_v3 was already IS_ENABLED()-guarded; the UFS
    FIPS self-test path is compiled only with SCSI_UFS_PIXEL_FIPS140.
  * vh_mm and pixel_stat_mm ARE built (they own /sys/kernel/vendor_mm and
    exports the dma-buf heap, mali and zram use); their registrations of
    hooks android-mainline lacks are fenced with "#if 0  junkyard ..." and
    the handlers marked __maybe_unused. pixel_stat_mm's CMA/direct-reclaim
    latency stats keep their per-task timestamp in two slots of
    task_struct.android_vendor_data1[] (pixel_stat_task.h) instead of
    vh_sched's vendor_task_struct. try_to_trigger_lmkd_kill() returns
    -EOPNOTSUPP: its tracepoint (and lmkd) do not exist here.
  * UFS inline-crypto: with FIPS140 off, the standard fill_prdt is
    registered (FIPS's self-test hook, android_rvh_ufs_complete_init, does
    not exist upstream).
  * PCIe RC: with use_linkup_irq gone, dw_pcie_host_init() always waits for
    link. A get_ltssm op reporting Detect.Quiet while the link is down turns
    that into the non-fatal -ENODEV ("Device not found") after ~1s, instead
    of touching a powered-down controller.
  * dma-buf chunk heap: ACK's gfp-taking __cma_alloc() -> cma_alloc(); the
    __GFP_NORETRY "fail fast" first attempt becomes a normal one.
  * xhci-exynos: the android_{rvh,vh}_usb_dev_{suspend,resume} calls were
    already under CONFIG_USB_VENDOR_HOOKS; the header include is now too.

Builds, links and passes modpost. Not run on hardware.

lynx-linus-mainline (android-mainline -> Linus' v7.3). The kernel is no
longer an Android Common Kernel, and the ACK-only interfaces these drivers
used are handled here instead of being restored in the kernel (see
kernel/patches/README.md, "lynx-linus-mainline").
IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ANDROID_VENDOR_HOOKS) is the "built against an ACK" test
throughout, so every changed site still builds the old way on an ACK.

Compatibility headers, include/linus-compat/ (new target
:linus_compat_headers; on the soc/gs Kbuild include path and in
Makefile.include, and given to every DDK module by device_build.bzl; always
searched after the kernel's own include/):
  * linux/of_gpio.h, linux/wakeup_reason.h: stand-ins for ACK-only headers.
    of_get_named_gpio() is rebuilt on of_parse_phandle_with_args() +
    gpio_device_find_by_fwnode() (standard two-cell xlate).
  * soc/google/linus-compat.h (force-included by Kbuild): strncpy() with its
    exact old semantics, trace_clock_set_rate() as a no-op,
    cpumap_print_to_pagebuf() -- all removed upstream.
  * soc/google/kernel-tracepoint.h: attach to unexported core tracepoints
    by name (for_each_kernel_tracepoint + tracepoint_probe_register), with a
    compile-time probe prototype check.
  * soc/google/sched-setscheduler.h, perf-read-local.h: the unexported
    sched_setscheduler[_nocheck]() and perf_event_read_local() rebuilt on
    exported API.
  * soc/google/samsung-dma-heap.h: in-kernel allocation from the Samsung
    heaps and per-attachment DMA attributes (below).

Ported to an upstream mechanism:
  * ufs: FMP software-keys mode fills the PRDT via the upstream
    .fill_crypto_prdt variant op (UFSHCD_QUIRK_KEYS_IN_PRDT), not
    android_vh_ufs_fill_prdt; use_kdn defaults to 0 and KDN (hardware-wrapped
    keys) mode disables inline crypto, since it needs the keyslot in the PRDT
    and GSA key restore via vendor hooks.
  * gs_perf_mon, devfreq-whi/arm-memlat-mon, hardlockup-debug: idle tracking
    on the exported power:cpu_idle tracepoint.
  * dma-buf heaps: each Samsung heap gets a faux device for cache maintenance
    (no dma_heap_get_dev()), keeps a heap list and exports
    samsung_dma_heap_find()/samsung_dma_heap_buffer_alloc() (no ACK
    dma_heap_find/_buffer_alloc/_put; heaps are never removed upstream), and
    keeps importers' DMA attributes in its per-attachment data (no
    dma_buf_attachment::dma_map_attrs). The partial cpu-access ops and
    get_flags (ACK-only dma_buf_ops) are not provided. mfc and smfc use the
    new calls.

Rebuilt from exported API (local copies of upstream's code):
dw_handle_msi_irq (PCIe dwc-whi MSI demux), thermal_cdev_update
(gs_thermal_compat.h), ufshcd_is_scsi_cmd, seq_put_decimal_ull_width,
thread_group_cputime_adjusted/nsec_to_clock_t (kernel-top). dump_backtrace
-> dump_stack_lvl/sched_show_task.

Compiled out (ACK-only, stats/debug/tuning; details at each site):
  * exynos-cpupm: android_vh_cpu_idle_* -- no next-hrtimer, so cluster/system
    power modes are never chosen from idle (per-core idle still works).
  * ufs-pixel: per-command hooks (I/O stats, command log, WriteBooster group
    tagging, sysfs refresh) and the UPIU query helpers behind the pixel UFS
    sysfs nodes (-EOPNOTSUPP); exynos-ufs: the vendor AH8 error interrupt
    and its hook.
  * s3c2410_wdt RT-load stat, debug-snapshot IPI-stop context save,
    sysrq-hook (module inert; sysrq-c panics upstream's way), hardlockup task
    dump, pixel_stat_mm CMA/direct-reclaim latency stats and pcpu pages,
    vh_mm per-CMA sysfs nodes.
  * tcpci_max77759: TCPM alternate-mode ignoring while the data path is
    disabled (GrapheneOS's tcpm_update_sink_capabilities()).
---
diff --git a/BUILD.bazel b/BUILD.bazel
index f764500..4861b82 100644
--- a/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/BUILD.bazel
@@ -97,6 +97,24 @@ filegroup(
     ],
 )
 
+# junkyard (lynx-linus-mainline): compatibility headers for building the
+# vendor modules against Linus' tree instead of an Android Common Kernel. Two
+# kinds (see each file):
+#   - stand-ins for headers the ACKs carry and Linus' tree does not
+#     (linux/of_gpio.h, linux/wakeup_reason.h);
+#   - soc/google/*.h replacements for unexported or removed core interfaces.
+# Given to every DDK module through the device kernel_build's
+# ddk_module_headers (private/devices/google/common/kleaf/device_build.bzl),
+# and to the soc/gs Kbuild through subdir-ccflags. `includes`, not
+# `linux_includes`: searched after the kernel's own include/, so a kernel
+# that does have one of these headers keeps its own.
+ddk_headers(
+    name = "linus_compat_headers",
+    hdrs = glob(["include/linus-compat/**/*.h"]),
+    includes = ["include/linus-compat"],
+    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
+)
+
 ddk_headers(
     name = "headers",
     hdrs = [":gs_soc_headers"],
diff --git a/Kbuild b/Kbuild
index e8faae6..f937b9f 100644
--- a/Kbuild
+++ b/Kbuild
@@ -3,6 +3,17 @@
 subdir-ccflags-y += \
 		-I$(src)/include \
 		-I$(src)/include/uapi \
+		-I$(src)/include/linus-compat \
+
+# junkyard (lynx, 6.18): much of the gs101/gs201-era code here predates
+# -Wmissing-prototypes being on by default (6.8) and CONFIG_WERROR. Keep the
+# warning, don't fail the build on it.
+subdir-ccflags-y += -Wno-error=missing-prototypes
+
+# junkyard (lynx-linus-mainline): interfaces Linus' tree removed that the
+# vendor code here still uses (strncpy(), the power:clock_set_rate event).
+# See the header.
+subdir-ccflags-y += -include $(src)/include/linus-compat/soc/google/linus-compat.h
 
 obj-y += drivers/phy/
 
diff --git a/Makefile.include b/Makefile.include
index 6197754..ffd123b 100644
--- a/Makefile.include
+++ b/Makefile.include
@@ -5,6 +5,10 @@
 
